From: pVisor maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] fuse: pipeline writeback with native dirty-page pressure

Keep native FUSE pagecache/writepages and negotiated request limits.
Account actual dirty and temporary WRITE pages rather than accumulated user
write bytes, including overwrites and aliases. The RAM/8 pressure target
is clamped to 16--256 MiB; native dirty throttling and reclaim still apply.
It is not a cap on clean guest pagecache or a crash-durability guarantee.

Separate best-effort data submission from the data-integrity completion
pass so a blocked inode does not serialize every later submission. Retain
the existing inode/handle leases through FLUSH, synchronous auto-submount
RELEASE and final reference disposal. Read-only close keeps native FLUSH.

